[metadata]
Name:P3b - the real g021 turn-50 board, with the lifelink blocker (control, and the round 1019 stall)
Description:The board as it was: Moldering Karok (lifelink) blocks, and the crocodile side has black mana for Stonefare Crocodile's lifelink. The best blocks let 10 through, but the Karok's lifelink gains 3 at the same time, so the opponent survives at 3 or more: alpha-strike-count must stay out. Round 1018 found what really stalled g021 for 20 turns: Forge's heuristic attacks with 20 here and takes the crocodiles to 3-6, but at lite and max Flat Monte Carlo overrides that with no attack (1667 vs 1380 on one rollout per line; on two per line in a warm JVM, the two samples identical). Round 1019's mc-attack-cut-guard keeps the heuristic's attack: with the rules on the AI attacks with at least 10, and survives the swing back (Turns:2 plays the crocodiles' turn). Rules off: the heuristic alone (off) attacks; lite and max hold back.
Turns:2
Expect:aiattackers>=10
Expect:ailife>=1
Expect:fired alpha-strike-count=0
RulesOff:off=pass,lite=fail,max=fail
